WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.409 --> 00:00:05.800
Classical conditioning is a way of
learning where a stimulus that triggers

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:10.570
a biological response is paired with a
new stimulus that then results in the

00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:15.840
same reaction.
The most famous work in classical

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:21.810
conditioning was done by Ivan Pavlov in
the 1890s. During this time Pavlov did a

00:00:21.810 --> 00:00:27.240
lot of research around the digestive
processes of dogs. One day during his

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:31.859
research Pavlov noticed that the dogs
began to salivate in the presence of the

00:00:31.859 --> 00:00:36.330
technician who normally fed them. He
wondered if the technician was a trigger

00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:44.400
that stimulated a response associated
with food? To find out he constructed an

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:49.290
experiment that would allow him to
measure a dog's output of saliva. First

00:00:49.290 --> 00:00:54.539
he served the dog food. Then he served
food while playing the sounds of a

00:00:54.539 --> 00:00:57.920
metronome and repeated the process a few
times.

00:00:57.920 --> 00:01:03.660
finally he removed the food and only
played the metronome. The dogs began to

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:08.729
salivate in response to the metronome
alone. Pavlov concluded that if a new

00:01:08.729 --> 00:01:13.350
stimulus was present when the dog was
given food then that stimulus became

00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:18.909
associated with food and caused salivation
on its own.

00:01:18.909 --> 00:01:23.740
When he published his findings Pavlov
called the food an "unconditioned

00:01:23.740 --> 00:01:29.079
stimulus" because its effects on the dog
were not learned instead they triggered

00:01:29.079 --> 00:01:33.549
an "unconditioned response" that happened
naturally and completely out of the

00:01:33.549 --> 00:01:39.429
dog's control. the metronome is at first
a "neutral stimulus" through the process

00:01:39.429 --> 00:01:44.890
of repetitive pairing with food the dog
learns to connect the two. This means

00:01:44.890 --> 00:01:49.780
that the "neutral stimulus" becomes the
"conditioned stimulus" and the response to

00:01:49.780 --> 00:01:57.429
that a "conditioned response". He also
reported that 1) learning occurred most

00:01:57.429 --> 00:02:01.689
rapidly when the interval between the
sound and the appearance of the food was

00:02:01.689 --> 00:02:07.390
short. 2) the saliva produced by the
sound differed in composition from that

00:02:07.390 --> 00:02:11.590
produced by the food, which means that
the conditioned response was not an

00:02:11.590 --> 00:02:17.170
exact replica of the unconditioned
response. 3) while there are several forms

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:21.760
of conditioning such as forward and
backward conditioning, classical

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:26.889
conditioning cannot create new behavior
or be used for training, but instead

00:02:26.889 --> 00:02:32.590
triggers involuntary biological
responses. 4) we can almost entirely

00:02:32.590 --> 00:02:37.389
undo the conditioning. This happens
through extinction: when we repeatedly

00:02:37.389 --> 00:02:43.840
present the conditioned stimulus in the
absence of the unconditioned stimulus.

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:49.989
So what occurs inside the brain? When a
dog sees the food the signals from the

00:02:49.989 --> 00:02:55.180
eyes and nose stimulate the brain which
activates the salivation glands to

00:02:55.180 --> 00:03:00.849
secrete saliva to aid the dog with the
digestion. When a dog hears a sound the

00:03:00.849 --> 00:03:06.069
ears send a signal to the brain which
takes note but has no reason to activate

00:03:06.069 --> 00:03:10.360
anything. When the two different
neurological processes are being

00:03:10.360 --> 00:03:15.819
activated simultaneously new synaptic
connections occur between the auditory

00:03:15.819 --> 00:03:21.040
stimulus and the behavioral response.
Over time these synapses are

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:25.660
strengthened so that it only takes the
sound to activate the pathway leading to

00:03:25.660 --> 00:03:30.800
salivation.
You can try this popular classroom

00:03:30.800 --> 00:03:37.190
exercise: take a friend, sit down and
relax for two minutes. Then allow your

00:03:37.190 --> 00:03:42.290
partner to check and record your pulse
rate. Your partner will then tap a pencil

00:03:42.290 --> 00:03:48.740
on the desk, five times. Right after stand
up and hop on one leg for 30 seconds and

00:03:48.740 --> 00:03:54.080
then check your pulse again! Repeat the
procedure four times having the partner

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:59.150
record all data. After relaxing for the
fifth time your partner will tap the

00:03:59.150 --> 00:04:04.670
pencil five times as usual now instead
of getting up for your exercise, only

00:04:04.670 --> 00:04:08.870
check your pulse.
If the conditioning was successful your

00:04:08.870 --> 00:04:14.480
pulse rate will rise even without
engaging in exercise!

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:19.820
What do you think does classical
conditioning always work? If so, are

00:04:19.820 --> 00:04:23.750
commercials a form of mental
manipulation and should we limit

00:04:23.750 --> 00:04:27.550
advertising in public spaces?

